================================================================================
Video and audio decoding — VLM gap-fill (runtime pip install)
================================================================================

The git release does not bundle codec binaries. AutoModel and Megatron-Bridge
launch scripts may download and install the packages below via pip into a
user-configurable cache directory (for example
${CACHE_DIR}/automodel_container_pkgs or
${CACHE_DIR}/megatron_bridge_container_pkgs) when they are missing from the
NeMo container. Set SKIP_VLM_TRAINING_DEPS=1 or SKIP_VLM_INFERENCE_DEPS=1 to
disable automatic installation.

When no system ffmpeg executable is available, scripts may expose the FFmpeg
binary shipped inside imageio-ffmpeg on PATH.

  decord              (pip)           Apache-2.0
  imageio-ffmpeg      (pip)           BSD-2-Clause
  librosa             (pip)           ISC
  audioread           (pip)           MIT
  pooch               (pip)           BSD-3-Clause
  lazy-loader         (pip)           BSD-3-Clause
  soundfile           (optional pip)  BSD-3-Clause

Sources:
  https://github.com/dmlc/decord
  https://github.com/imageio/imageio-ffmpeg
  https://github.com/librosa/librosa
  https://github.com/beetbox/audioread
  https://github.com/fatiando/pooch
  https://github.com/scientific-python/lazy_loader
  https://github.com/bastibe/python-soundfile

decord depends on FFmpeg/libav at runtime for video decoding.

